  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 253 PM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nMuch cooler air filters into the area Sunday night as strong low-\nlevel CAA continues within this post-frontal airmass. An Arctic \nsurface high will slowly slide southeast out of Canada, not nearing \nthe area until the middle of next week. The result will be northerly \nflow that brings continued CAA keeping temperatures 5-10 degrees \nbelow average. Given the near record warmth we are currently \nexperiencing, this will be quite the change as this airmass will be \nabout 30 degrees colder when it comes to afternoon highs. Guidance \nis also in good agreement that lows will be below average also with \nwidespread 20s and possibly some teens each morning through the \nmiddle of next week. There is also increasing agreement with \nguidance that a shortwave traverses into the region sometime between \nWednesday Thursday. However there is a lot of variance with the \namplitude and timing of this feature, which is resulting in low \nconfidence regarding chances for precipitation around the middle of \nnext week. What is more certain is that temperatures are expected to \nremain below normal through Wednesday and possibly into next\nFriday.",
